Quality of life: in-game changes are kept, the game pauses when it loses
focus, fast-forward can toggle, and the Home menu's IMAGE FIT row works on
every preset.

Kept changes (PSX_MENU_PREFS_FILE). The Home menu's GAME ASPECT, IMAGE FIT,
WINDOW MODE, FPS DISPLAY, POST FX, 99 LIVES and AKU AKU rows, the F readout
key and the volume keys used to change only the running game ("MENU CHANGES
APPLY NOW BUT RESET ON NEXT LAUNCH"). With the variable set - the launcher
passes a file in its userdata folder - every value changed this session is
written there as JSON under the launcher's own setting names (aspect,
scaling_mode, fullscreen_mode, fps_overlay, postfx_enabled,
cheat_infinite_lives, cheat_aku_aku, volume), and the launcher folds it into
its settings when the game exits. Only values the player touched are written.
The file is written when the menu closes and first thing in shutdown_runtime,
never from the frame path, via a temp file and MoveFileExW. The footer says
"CHANGES HERE ARE KEPT FOR NEXT TIME" (psx_pause_menu_set_persistent).

IMAGE FIT takes the framing over. The launcher's Zoom and Stretch dials decide
the present rect whenever they are set (letterbox_rect_aspect), so on the
Enhanced preset (zoom 0, stretch 100) LETTERBOX, STRETCH and FILL drew the
same picture. pause_menu_apply_fit now also sets zoom -1 and stretch 0, so
each value looks like its name, and the kept change clears them too. POST FX
with no effect configured (the row reads NONE) no longer flips hidden state.

Pause on focus loss (PSX_PAUSE_ON_FOCUS_LOSS=1): losing window focus opens the
Home menu once the game has started, outside netplay and other modals. While
the window is unfocused the menu ignores the pad, so a controller used in
another window cannot resume the game.

Fast-forward toggle (PSX_FAST_FORWARD_TOGGLE=1): the fast-forward key switches
it on and off instead of being held; PSX_FAST_FORWARD_SPEED keeps the cap.

Restart through the launcher (PSX_RESTART_EXIT_CODE): RESTART GAME exits with
that code instead of re-spawning itself, so the launcher, which could not see
the re-spawned process, restarts it and keeps tracking the game.

gpu_postfx.c: PSX_POSTFX_ENABLED=0 starts with the effects off while still
loading them, so the POST FX row can switch them on. postfx_enabled/
set_enabled/active/dedither_active read the environment first, so an early
toggle cannot be overwritten by it.

Release builds no longer eject the disc on Ctrl+C (a debug-build aid, now
under #ifndef PSX_NO_DEBUG_TOOLS, with its Spanish log line in English), and
the host refresh log prints SDL3's float refresh rate as a float.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

